nfstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-7kBdOJxp' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-01 19:13:59.362 xcodebuild[21803:36923131]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-01 19:13:59.653 xcodebuild[21803:36923130] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-SF17gFN6' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-01 19:14:00.314 xcodebuild[21808:36923157]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-01 19:14:00.568 xcodebuild[21808:36923156] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ncommit 7a8493e1f283b9f6614556808e03348a90627076\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Thu Oct 1 19:13:03 2026 +0700\n\n    feat(yang.python): Python phase C1 — finally/with, tuples and slices, full operators, comprehensions, keyword arguments\n    \n    finally runs on every exit (normal, return, break, continue, raise) through\n    depth-numbered handler frames that escapes unwind; with follows the\n    reference expansion. Tuples have value semantics and hash as keys;\n    unpacking supports nesting and one star target; slices follow\n    slice.indices with slice assignment on lists. Operators gain ** // % and\n    bitwise ops with Python semantics, in / not in, and in-place list += and\n    *=; any int result outside +-2^53 raises OverflowError identically on\n    every host. Comprehensions get their own scope (first iterable in the\n    enclosing scope); generator expressions are accepted only as the sole\n    argument of a consuming builtin. Calls take keyword arguments, *args and\n    **kwargs, with keyword-only parameters and Python's TypeErrors. except\n    and isinstance accept tuples of classes; raise requires a BaseException;\n    except ... as e unbinds e; range len/membership are O(1); dict and set\n    iteration that changes size raises RuntimeError.\n    \n    Gate: qwen3.8-max r1 REQUEST CHANGES, fixed in round 2.\n\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc           |  737 +++++++++++-----\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc         | 1080 ++++++++++++++++++++---\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc          |   42 +-\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/scope.cljc           |  161 +++-\n test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj          |  501 +++++++++++\n test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj             |    2 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc |    4 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj           |  190 +++-\n test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc |   73 ++\n test/yang/python/antlr/scope_test.clj           |   44 +\n 10 files changed, 2433 insertions(+), 401 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
