{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.python.antlr.prelude\n     2\t  \"The Python runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n     3\t   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §8.1, §8.2, §9.3). Python semantics for\n     4\t   operators, truthiness, equality, objects, exceptions and escapes live\n     5\t   here as guest code, not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications\n     6\t   of these names.\n     7\t\n     8\t   Value encoding:\n     9\t     int             host integer (untagged)\n    10\t     float           {:py/float x}: tagged on every host, because JS cannot\n    11\t                     tell 2 from 2.0 (owner decision 3)\n    12\t     bool            host true / false (numeric as 1 / 0)\n    13\t     None            :py/None\n    14\t     str             {:py/str \\\"...\\\"}\n    15\t     list            a cell holding {:py/type :list :items [...]}\n    16\t     dict            a cell holding {:py/type :dict :index {nkey slot}\n    17\t                     :keys [...] :vals [...]}: insertion order is the keys\n    18\t                     vector, never a host map's order; keys are normalized\n    19\t                     so 1, 1.0 and True are one key\n    20\t     set             a cell holding {:py/type :set :index {nkey slot}\n    21\t                     :keys [...]}: insertion order, keys normalized as for\n    22\t                     dicts\n    23\t     function        a cell holding {:py/type :function :name s :spec spec\n    24\t                     :defaults [...] :kwdefaults [[name v] ...]\n    25\t                     :code (fn [args] ...)}; identity is the cell ref\n    26\t     class           a cell holding {:py/type :class :name s :base cls\n    27\t                     :attrs {name value}}\n    28\t     instance        a cell holding {:py/type :instance :class cls\n    29\t                     :attrs {name value}}\n    30\t     bound method    {:py/type :method :self obj :fn function}\n    31\t     tuple           {:py/type :tuple :items [...]}: a value; hashable when\n    32\t                     its elements are\n    33\t     slice           {:py/type :slice :start a :stop b :step c}\n    34\t     range           {:py/type :range :start a :stop b :step s}\n    35\t     module globals  a dict (owner decision 1): the module body receives it\n    36\t                     as `%globals` and every function closes over it, which\n    37\t                     is Python's own `__globals__`; a miss is NameError\n    38\t\n    39\t   Calling convention: a function's `:code` takes one vector of arguments\n    40\t   laid out as the parameters are written. `py/call-kw` (and `py/call`,\n    41\t   its positional-only form) binds positional arguments, keywords, defaults,\n    42\t   `*args` and `**kwargs` from the function's static spec; every binding\n    43\t   failure is a Python TypeError.\n    44\t\n    45\t   Runtime state is two cells, reached through the store (`yin/def` is\n    46\t   reserved for the prelude and builtins):\n    47\t     py.rt/handlers  the handler stack: frames [kind payload rest depth];\n    48\t                     a :handler frame holds the continuation `raise`\n    49\t                     delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every exit\n    50\t                     through it runs (raise passes the exception, escapes\n    51\t                     and normal completion pass None); nil when empty\n    52\t     py.rt/out       the values `print` collected, one vector per call\n    53\t\n    54\t   Escapes and handlers tell the first pass through a capture point from a\n    55\t   re-entry with a flag cell allocated before the capture (`:first`, then\n    56\t   `:re-entered`): heap writes survive continuation invocation, so the flag\n    57\t   answers without inspecting the continuation's representation. An escape\n    58\t   unwinds to the depth it captured, running finally thunks on the way.\n    59\t\n    60\t   Integer `//`, `%`, `**`, bitwise operators and float floor have no\n    61\t   portable host primitive; they are exact algorithms here over + - * <\n    62\t   (doubling division, binary-descent floor, two's-complement recursion),\n    63\t   valid within 2^53.\n    64\t\n    65\t   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n    66\t   (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n    67\t  (:require\n    68\t    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def host-names\n    72\t  \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n    73\t  '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/into data/subvec\n    74\t     data/str-concat data/str-length data/str-index-of data/str->code-points\n    75\t     data/code-points->str})\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def ^:private core-definitions\n    79\t  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n    80\t  '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n    81\t    [py/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n    82\t    [py/str? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/str))))]\n    83\t    [py/str (fn [s] (assoc {} :py/str s))]\n    84\t    [py/float? (fn [x] (not (nil? (get x :py/float))))]\n    85\t    [py/float (fn [x] (assoc {} :py/float (* 1.0 x)))]\n    86\t    [py/tuple (fn [items] (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :tuple) :items items))]\n    87\t    [py/conj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n    88\t    [py/arg (fn [args i] (get args i))]\n    89\t    [py/numeric?\n    90\t     (fn [x]\n    91\t       (if (= x true)\n    92\t         true\n    93\t         (if (= x false) true (if (py/float? x) true (data/number? x)))))]\n    94\t    [py/num\n    95\t     (fn [x]\n    96\t       (if (= x true) 1 (if (= x false) 0 (if (py/float? x) (get x :py/float) x))))]\n    97\t    [py/zero? (fn [x] (let [v (py/num x)] (if (= v 0) true (= v 0.0))))]\n    98\t    [py/content-type (fn [x] (if (py/cell? x) (get (cell/get x) :py/type) nil))]\n    99\t    [py/function? (fn [x] (= (py/content-type x) :function))]\n   100\t\n   101\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n   102\t    ;; The handler stack is a chain of frames [kind payload rest depth]:\n   103\t    ;; :handler frames hold the continuation `raise` delivers to, :finally\n   104\t    ;; frames hold a thunk of one argument (the exception, or None) that\n   105\t    ;; every exit through them runs. Depth makes \"unwind to here\" an integer\n   106\t    ;; comparison.\n   107\t    [py/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n   108\t    [py/frame\n   109\t     (fn [kind payload rest]\n   110\t       (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] kind) payload) rest)\n   111\t                (+ 1 (py/frame-depth rest))))]\n   112\t    [py/raise\n   113\t     (fn [e]\n   114\t       (let [hs (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n   115\t         (if (nil? hs)\n   116\t           (:py/no-handler e)\n   117\t           (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n   118\t             (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (get hs 2))\n   119\t                 ((get hs 1) e)\n   120\t                 (py/raise e))\n   121\t             ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n   122\t    [py/unwind-to\n   123\t     ;; pop frames above depth d, running each finally thunk with None\n   124\t     (fn [d]\n   125\t       (let [hs (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n   126\t         (if (nil? hs)\n   127\t           :py/None\n   128\t           (if (<= (get hs 3) d)\n   129\t             :py/None\n   130\t             (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (get hs 2))\n   131\t                 (if (= (get hs 0) :finally) ((get hs 1) :py/None) :py/None)\n   132\t                 (py/unwind-to d))))))]\n   133\t    [py/try\n   134\t     (fn [body handler orelse]\n   135\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)\n   136\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n   137\t         ((fn [r]\n   138\t            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n   139\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n   140\t                  (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (py/frame :handler r saved))\n   141\t                  (body)\n   142\t                  (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n   143\t                  (orelse))\n   144\t              (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n   145\t                  (handler r))))\n   146\t          (%capture))))]\n   147\t    [py/try-finally\n   148\t     ;; normal exit runs `fin` here; raise and escapes run it as they\n   149\t     ;; unwind through the :finally frame\n   150\t     (fn [body fin]\n   151\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)]\n   152\t         (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers (py/frame :finally fin saved))\n   153\t             (let [v (body)]\n   154\t               (do (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n   155\t                   (fin :py/None)\n   156\t                   v)))))]\n   157\t    [py/call-ec\n   158\t     (fn [f]\n   159\t       (let [saved (cell/get py.rt/handlers)\n   160\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n   161\t         ((fn [r]\n   162\t            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n   163\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n   164\t                  (f (fn [x]\n   165\t                       (do (py/unwind-to (py/frame-depth saved))\n   166\t                           (cell/set! py.rt/handlers saved)\n   167\t                           (r x)))))\n   168\t              r))\n   169\t          (%capture))))]\n   170\t    [py/type-of\n   171\t     (fn [x] (if (= (py/content-type x) :instance) (get (cell/get x) :class) :py/None))]\n   172\t    [py/with\n   173\t     ;; the language reference's expansion: __exit__ is looked up before\n   174\t     ;; __enter__ runs; an exception calls __exit__(type, value, None) and\n   175\t     ;; is suppressed when that is truthy; every other exit calls\n   176\t     ;; __exit__(None, None, None)\n   177\t     ;; Both dunders are looked up on the manager's type, as implicit\n   178\t     ;; invocations are; an instance attribute of that name is not used.\n   179\t     (fn [mgr suite]\n   180\t       (let [cls (py/type-of mgr)\n   181\t             enter-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__enter__\"))\n   182\t             exit-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__exit__\"))]\n   183\t         (if (if (= enter-fn :py/missing) true (= exit-fn :py/missing))\n   184\t           (py/type-error\n   185\t             {:py/str \"object does not support the context manager protocol\"})\n   186\t           (py/with-bound mgr (py/bind mgr enter-fn) (py/bind mgr exit-fn) suite))))]\n   187\t    [py/with-bound\n   188\t     (fn [mgr enter exit suite]\n   189\t       (let [value (py/call enter [])\n   190\t             hit (cell/new false)]\n   191\t         (py/try-finally\n   192\t           (fn []\n   193\t             (py/try (fn [] (suite value))\n   194\t                     (fn [e]\n   195\t                       (do (cell/set! hit true)\n   196\t                           (if (py/truthy\n   197\t                                 (py/call exit\n   198\t                                          (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] (py/type-of e)) e)\n   199\t                                                   :py/None)))\n   200\t                             :py/None\n   201\t                             (py/raise e))))\n   202\t                     (fn [] :py/None)))\n   203\t           (fn [x]\n   204\t             (if (cell/get hit)\n   205\t               :py/None\n   206\t               (py/call exit (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] :py/None) :py/None)\n   207\t                                      :py/None)))))))]\n   208\t\n   209\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- exceptions\n   210\t    [py/make-class\n   211\t     (fn [name base]\n   212\t       (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :class) :name name)\n   213\t                               :base base)\n   214\t                        :attrs {})))]\n   215\t    [py/make-instance\n   216\t     (fn [cls]\n   217\t       (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :instance) :class cls)\n   218\t                        :attrs {})))]\n   219\t    [py/make-exc\n   220\t     (fn [cls msg]\n   221\t       (let [e (py/make-instance cls)]\n   222\t         (do (py/setattr e \"args\" (py/tuple (py/conj [] msg))) e)))]\n   223\t    [py/raise-new (fn [cls msg] (py/raise (py/make-exc cls msg)))]\n   224\t    [py/type-error (fn [msg] (py/raise-new py.b/TypeError msg))]\n   225\t    [py/as-exception\n   226\t     ;; `raise X`: a BaseException subclass is instantiated, an instance of\n   227\t     ;; one is raised as is, anything else is a TypeError\n   228\t     (fn [x]\n   229\t       (let [t (py/content-type x)]\n   230\t         (if (if (= t :class) (py/subclass? x py.b/BaseException) false)\n   231\t           (py/call x [])\n   232\t           (if (if (= t :instance)\n   233\t                 (py/subclass? (get (cell/get x) :class) py.b/BaseException)\n   234\t                 false)\n   235\t             x\n   236\t             (py/type-error {:py/str \"exceptions must derive from BaseException\"})))))]\n   237\t    [py/subclass?\n   238\t     (fn [c target]\n   239\t       (if (= c :py/None)\n   240\t         false\n   241\t         (if (= c target) true (py/subclass? (get (cell/get c) :base) target))))]\n   242\t    [py/class-match?\n   243\t     ;; c (a class, or None) against target: a class, or a tuple of classes\n   244\t     ;; and tuples, matched recursively. A target that is neither is a\n   245\t     ;; TypeError `msg`; with `exc?` a class must also derive from\n   246\t     ;; BaseException, as an except clause requires.\n   247\t     (fn [c target exc? msg]\n   248\t       (if (= (get target :py/type) :tuple)\n   249\t         (py/any-class-match? c (get target :items) 0 exc? msg)\n   250\t         (if (= (py/content-type target) :class)\n   251\t           (if (if exc? (not (py/subclass? target py.b/BaseException)) false)\n   252\t             (py/type-error msg)\n   253\t             (py/subclass? c target))\n   254\t           (py/type-error msg))))]\n   255\t    [py/any-class-match?\n   256\t     (fn [c ts i exc? msg]\n   257\t       (let [t (get ts i :py/stop)]\n   258\t         (if (= t :py/stop)\n   259\t           false\n   260\t           (if (py/class-match? c t exc? msg)\n   261\t             true\n   262\t             (py/any-class-match? c ts (+ i 1) exc? msg)))))]\n   263\t    [py/isinstance\n   264\t     (fn [o cls]\n   265\t       (py/class-match? (py/type-of o) cls false\n   266\t                        {:py/str \"isinstance() arg 2 must be a type or tuple of types\"}))]\n   267\t    [py/exc-class?\n   268\t     (fn [x] (if (= (py/content-type x) :class) (py/subclass? x py.b/BaseException) false))]\n   269\t    [py/all-exc-classes?\n   270\t     (fn [ts i]\n   271\t       (let [t (get ts i :py/stop)]\n   272\t         (if (= t :py/stop) true (if (py/exc-class? t) (py/all-exc-classes? ts (+ i 1)) false))))]\n   273\t    [py/exc-matches\n   274\t     ;; an except clause's test of the exception in flight, as CPython does\n   275\t     ;; it: a BaseException subclass, or a flat tuple of them, every element\n   276\t     ;; checked before any is matched; anything else (a nested tuple\n   277\t     ;; included) is a TypeError\n   278\t     (fn [e cls]\n   279\t       (if (if (= (get cls :py/type) :tuple)\n   280\t             (py/all-exc-classes? (get cls :items) 0)\n   281\t             (py/exc-class? cls))\n   282\t         (py/class-match? (py/type-of e) cls true {:py/str \"\"})\n   283\t         (py/type-error {:py/str (data/str-concat\n   284\t                                   \"catching classes that do not inherit from \"\n   285\t                                   \"BaseException is not allowed\")})))]\n   286\t\n   287\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- names\n   288\t    [py/local-get\n   289\t     (fn [c n]\n   290\t       (let [x (cell/get c)]\n   291\t         (if (= x :py/unbound)\n   292\t           (py/raise-new py.b/UnboundLocalError\n   293\t                         (py/str (data/str-concat\n   294\t                                   \"cannot access local variable '\" (get n :py/str)\n   295\t                                   \"' where it is not associated with a value\")))\n   296\t           x)))]\n   297\t    [py/global-get\n   298\t     (fn [g n]\n   299\t       (let [c (cell/get g)\n   300\t             slot (get (get c :index) n :py/missing)]\n   301\t         (if (= slot :py/missing)\n   302\t           (py/raise-new py.b/NameError\n   303\t                         (py/str (data/str-concat \"name '\" (get n :py/str)\n   304\t                                                  \"' is not defined\")))\n   305\t           (get (get c :vals) slot))))]\n   306\t    [py/global-set (fn [g n x] (do (py/dict-set g n x) :py/None))]\n   307\t    [py/global-or\n   308\t     ;; a builtin name: the module's binding when present, else the builtin\n   309\t     (fn [g n builtin]\n   310\t       (let [c (cell/get g)\n   311\t             slot (get (get c :index) n :py/missing)]\n   312\t         (if (= slot :py/missing) builtin (get (get c :vals) slot))))]\n   313\t    [py/class-ns-get\n   314\t     ;; a name assigned in a class body, read in that body: the class\n   315\t     ;; namespace as it is now, else `fallback` (globals, then builtins)\n   316\t     (fn [cls name fallback]\n   317\t       (let [x (get (get (cell/get cls) :attrs) name :py/missing)]\n   318\t         (if (= x :py/missing) (fallback) x)))]\n   319\t\n   320\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- functions\n   321\t    ;; A function's `spec` is static data from the lowering:\n   322\t    ;;   {:params [positional names] :star? bool :kwonly [names] :kwstar? bool}\n   323\t    ;; `defaults` holds the trailing positional defaults and `kwdefaults`\n   324\t    ;; [[name value] ...] the keyword-only ones, both evaluated at\n   325\t    ;; definition time. `code` takes one vector laid out as the parameters\n   326\t    ;; are written: positional, the *args tuple, keyword-only, the **kwargs\n   327\t    ;; dict.\n   328\t    [py/make-function\n   329\t     (fn [name spec defaults kwdefaults code]\n   330\t       (cell/new (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :function)\n   331\t                                                    :name name)\n   332\t                                             :spec spec)\n   333\t                                      :defaults defaults)\n   334\t                               :kwdefaults kwdefaults)\n   335\t                        :code code)))]\n   336\t    [py/fn-error\n   337\t     (fn [fc msg] (py/type-error (py/str (data/str-concat (get fc :name) msg))))]\n   338\t    [py/index-of\n   339\t     (fn [xs x i]\n   340\t       (let [y (get xs i :py/stop)]\n   341\t         (if (= y :py/stop) -1 (if (= y x) i (py/index-of xs x (+ i 1))))))]\n   342\t    [py/pad\n   343\t     ;; the first n of xs, :py/missing where xs is shorter\n   344\t     (fn [xs n i acc]\n   345\t       (if (< i n) (py/pad xs n (+ i 1) (conj acc (get xs i :py/missing))) acc))]\n   346\t    [py/bind-keyword\n   347\t     ;; state is [positional-slots kwonly-slots kwargs-dict-or-nil]\n   348\t     (fn [fc state name x]\n   349\t       (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n   350\t             pi (py/index-of (get spec :params) name 0)\n   351\t             ki (py/index-of (get spec :kwonly) name 0)\n   352\t             dup (py/str (data/str-concat \"() got multiple values for argument '\"\n   353\t                                          name \"'\"))]\n   354\t         (if (< -1 pi)\n   355\t           (if (= (get (get state 0) pi) :py/missing)\n   356\t             (assoc state 0 (assoc (get state 0) pi x))\n   357\t             (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n   358\t           (if (< -1 ki)\n   359\t             (if (= (get (get state 1) ki) :py/missing)\n   360\t               (assoc state 1 (assoc (get state 1) ki x))\n   361\t               (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str)))\n   362\t             (if (nil? (get state 2))\n   363\t               (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n   364\t                                 \"() got an unexpected keyword argument '\" name \"'\"))\n   365\t               (if (py/dict-has? (get state 2) (py/str name))\n   366\t                 (py/fn-error fc (get dup :py/str))\n   367\t                 (do (py/dict-set (get state 2) (py/str name) x) state)))))))]\n   368\t    [py/bind-keywords\n   369\t     (fn [fc state kwargs i]\n   370\t       (let [pair (get kwargs i :py/stop)]\n   371\t         (if (= pair :py/stop)\n   372\t           state\n   373\t           (py/bind-keywords fc (py/bind-keyword fc state (get pair 0) (get pair 1))\n   374\t                             kwargs (+ i 1)))))]\n   375\t    [py/fill-defaults\n   376\t     (fn [fc slots defaults n i]\n   377\t       (if (< i n)\n   378\t         (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n   379\t           (let [j (- i (- n (data/count defaults)))]\n   380\t             (if (< j 0)\n   381\t               (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n   382\t                                 \"() missing required positional argument '\"\n   383\t                                 (get (get (get fc :spec) :params) i) \"'\"))\n   384\t               (py/fill-defaults fc (assoc slots i (get defaults j)) defaults n\n   385\t                                 (+ i 1))))\n   386\t           (py/fill-defaults fc slots defaults n (+ i 1)))\n   387\t         slots))]\n   388\t    [py/lookup-pair\n   389\t     (fn [pairs name i]\n   390\t       (let [pair (get pairs i :py/stop)]\n   391\t         (if (= pair :py/stop)\n   392\t           :py/missing\n   393\t           (if (= (get pair 0) name) (get pair 1) (py/lookup-pair pairs name (+ i 1))))))]\n   394\t    [py/fill-kwdefaults\n   395\t     (fn [fc slots names i]\n   396\t       (let [nm (get names i :py/stop)]\n   397\t         (if (= nm :py/stop)\n   398\t           slots\n   399\t           (if (= (get slots i) :py/missing)\n   400\t             (let [d (py/lookup-pair (get fc :kwdefaults) nm 0)]\n   401\t               (if (= d :py/missing)\n   402\t                 (py/fn-error fc (data/str-concat\n   403\t                                   \"() missing required keyword-only argument '\"\n   404\t                                   nm \"'\"))\n   405\t                 (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (assoc slots i d) names (+ i 1))))\n   406\t             (py/fill-kwdefaults fc slots names (+ i 1))))))]\n   407\t    [py/bind-args\n   408\t     ;; positional, then keywords, then defaults; every failure a TypeError\n   409\t     (fn [fc args kwargs]\n   410\t       (let [spec (get fc :spec)\n   411\t             n (data/count (get spec :params))\n   412\t             given (data/count args)\n   413\t             star (get spec :star?)]\n   414\t         (if (if (get spec :no-kw) (< 0 (data/count kwargs)) false)\n   415\t           (py/fn-error fc \"() takes no keyword arguments\")\n   416\t           (if (if (< n given) (not star) false)\n   417\t             (py/fn-error fc \"() takes too many positional arguments\")\n   418\t             (let [state (py/bind-keywords\n   419\t                           fc\n   420\t                           (py/conj (py/conj (py/conj [] (py/pad args n 0 []))\n   421\t                                             (py/pad [] (data/count (get spec :kwonly)) 0 []))\n   422\t                                    (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/dict-new) nil))\n   423\t                           kwargs\n   424\t                           0)\n   425\t                   slots (py/fill-defaults fc (get state 0) (get fc :defaults) n 0)\n   426\t                   ko (py/fill-kwdefaults fc (get state 1) (get spec :kwonly) 0)\n   427\t                   with-star (if star\n   428\t                               (py/conj slots\n   429\t                                        (py/tuple (if (< n given) (data/subvec args n) [])))\n   430\t                               slots)\n   431\t                   with-ko (data/into with-star ko)]\n   432\t               (if (get spec :kwstar?) (py/conj with-ko (get state 2)) with-ko))))))]\n   433\t    [py/call (fn [f args] (py/call-kw f args []))]\n   434\t    [py/call-kw\n   435\t     (fn [f args kwargs]\n   436\t       (if (= (get f :py/type) :method)\n   437\t         (py/call-kw (get f :fn) (data/into (py/conj [] (get f :self)) args) kwargs)\n   438\t         (let [t (py/content-type f)]\n   439\t           (if (= t :function)\n   440\t             (let [fc (cell/get f)] ((get fc :code) (py/bind-args fc args kwargs)))\n   441\t             (if (= t :class)\n   442\t               (py/instantiate f args kwargs)\n   443\t               (py/type-error {:py/str \"object is not callable\"}))))))]\n   444\t    [py/instantiate\n   445\t     (fn [cls args kwargs]\n   446\t       (let [inst (py/make-instance cls)\n   447\t             init (py/class-lookup cls \"__init__\")]\n   448\t         ;; without __init__ only exception classes take arguments (they\n   449\t         ;; become `args`); any other class takes none\n   450\t         (do (if (= init :py/missing)\n   451\t               (if (py/subclass? cls py.b/BaseException)\n   452\t                 (py/setattr inst \"args\" (py/tuple args))\n   453\t                 (if (if (< 0 (data/count args)) true (< 0 (data/count kwargs)))\n   454\t                   (py/type-error\n   455\t                     (py/str (data/str-concat (get (cell/get cls) :name)\n   456\t                                              \"() takes no arguments\")))\n   457\t                   :py/None))\n   458\t               (py/call-kw init (data/into (py/conj [] inst) args) kwargs))\n   459\t             inst)))]\n   460\t    [py/extend\n   461\t     ;; call-site *iterabl