{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat deps.edn | tail -100; sed -n '1,130p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790852251711-reviewer-python-phase-c1-gate.qwen3.8-max.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl.main/-main\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yang.python-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: 735ea0f5-f108-41aa-8a10-0f9221aa416e\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-01 11:31:42 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-01 18:31:42 +07\n\nRead-only review of the uncommitted diff on `yang-python-phase-c1` (lower/prelude/render/scope + tests + new `e2e_c1_test.clj`), against the language reference, the two architect rulings, the r2 gate findings, and the C1 brief. Orchestrator-verified checks not rerun; report treated as untrusted and re-derived from source.\n\n**Verified clean** (evidence in files): finally on every exit incl. return-override, raise-replacement, nesting order, break/continue-through-finally via depth-numbered frames (`prelude.cljc:112-207`, escapes always `unwind-to` before jumping, thunks run with their own frame popped — no double-run); `with` per reference expansion (`__exit__` looked up before `__enter__`, `(type, value, None)`, truthy suppresses, `__enter__` failure skips `__exit__`, `hit` prevents double `__exit__`, nesting exits in reverse — e2e lines 119-150); slice clamping matches `slice.indices` incl. negative steps and defaults (`prelude.cljc:895-921`); `//`, `%` floor/sign rules exact for ints (`-7//2=-4`, `7%-3=-2` pinned in parity test); two's-complement bitwise on negatives (`-6&3=2`); negative shift → ValueError; `**` right-regrouping, `2**-1=0.5`, `0**-n`→ZeroDivisionError, `-2**2=-4` (grammar alt order confirmed: `**` outranks unary, `Python3Parser.g4:563-573`); tuple value semantics + recursive key normalization (`(1,2)`≡`(1.0,2)`, unhashable→TypeError); star unpack (middle is a list), count→ValueError; list `+=`/`*=` aliasing via cell mutation; comprehension scope split (first iterable in enclosing/class scope, lambda capture `[2,2,2]`, nested-comp registration); genexp only for `list/tuple/set/sum/any/all` resolved-as-builtin (excluding `len` is *more* correct than the brief — `len(genexp)` is TypeError in CPython); keyword binding all-TypeError matrix tested e2e; kwonly defaults at def time; every grammar rule classified (disjoint union test); no host-map iteration (dicts/sets walk `:keys`/`:vals` vectors; `:index` is lookup-only); no gensym/rand, generated names from node ids; `data/count nil`=0 keeps the no-kwonly spec path safe; P3 dispositions (a)-(e) all check out — (a) matches CPython (interpreter-raised errors and the implicit base are `builtins.*` regardless of module bindings, pinned by `gate-p3-runtime-test`), (d) lexer-level `0755` rejection pinned plus a lowering guard, `00` still valid; new `code-unit` reader conditional has `:cljd` first; chunk invariance re-tested.\n\n**Findings**\n\n- **P1 | prelude.cljc:232-241 + lower.cljc:1202-1206 | Tuple of classes never matches, silently.** `py/subclass?` compares the class cell to `target` with `=`; a tuple target (`{:py/type :tuple …}`) is never equal, so `except (A, B):` never catches (the exception propagates past the handler to re-raise) and `isinstance(x, (A, B))` returns False where CPython returns True. Both forms are standard language-reference syntax inside the *claimed* try/except and isinstance support; they are neither correct nor rejected with a qualified diagnostic, violating \"nothing is silently dropped\". No test covers it (grep `except \\(` across test/: zero hits). Pre-existing from the spike, but in this gate's scope. **Fix:** in `py/isinstance`, when `(= (get cls :py/type) :tuple)`, walk `:items` and match any (reuse `py/seq-contains?`-style recursion over `py/subclass?`); alternatively reject a tuple class-expression in `except_clause`/isinstance at lowering with a qualified diagnostic. Add an e2e case on all four VMs (`except (KeyError, ValueError)` catching each, `isinstance(1, (int, str))`-style with user classes).\n\n- **P2 | prelude.cljc:632-639, 690, 489-496 (over vm.cljc:360-363) | The 2^53 integer bound is documented but unenforced, and crossing it diverges per host.** VM primitives `*`/`+` are host ops: JVM throws `ArithmeticException` (a host error outside guest diagnostics), CLJS doubles go silently inexact above 2^53, CLJD/Dart wraps at 64 bits. Reachable with fully supported syntax: `print(2 ** 53 + 1)` → `…993` on JVM, `…992` on Node; `print(3 ** 40)` → exact on JVM, inexact on Node, wrapped on Dart; `1 << 63` → JVM host crash, Node fine. This breaks the determinism/parity invariant on accepted programs; `py/floor` (prelude.cljc:597-607) already sets the precedent of a uniform guest `OverflowError`. **Fix:** magnitude guards raising guest `OverflowError` when an int result leaves ±2^53 — minimally in `py/ipow`'s multiply step, `py/lshift`, and `py/arith`'s int path (which also covers `+`/`*`/pre-existing exposure); add parity cases at the boundary (`2**53`, `2**53+1`, `3**40`, `1<<62` vs `1<<63`).\n\n- **P3 | lower.cljc:1144-1157 | `break`/`continue` inside a `finally` clause is accepted.** The finally thunk is lowered with the loop context intact; Python 3.8+ rejects this at compile time (`'break'/'continue' inside 'finally' clause`). Runs \"plausibly\" here, so an invalid program is silently accepted. **Fix:** `syntax!` when the finally block `contains-rule?` break/continue (stop at scope rules), or record as an accepted deviation in the design notes.\n\n- **P3 | prelude.cljc:225-231, 237-241; lower.cljc:1195-1199 | Exception-protocol laxness.** `py/as-exception` accepts *any* cell (`raise [1,2]`, `raise C()` for non-BaseException `C`) where Python raises TypeError \"exceptions must derive from BaseException\"; a non-class except expression (`except None:`) silently never matches instead of TypeError at match time; `except E as e:` leaves `e` bound after the block (Python deletes it). **Fix:** in `as-exception` require content-type `:instance` and `py/subclass? … py.b/BaseException`; type-check the clause expression when matching; emit a reset-to-unbound after the handler block.\n\n- **P3 | prelude.cljc:757-758, 1008-1009 | `in range(...)` and `len(range(...))` are O(n).** `py/contains` materializes via `py/to-vector`; `py/range-len` iterates. `len(range(2**40))` or `x in range(10**12)` hangs where CPython is O(1) — a guest-reachable hang with legal literals. **Fix:** closed forms — len `max(0, ceil((stop-start)/step))` via existing `py/int-floordiv`; membership `start<=x<stop` (sign-adjusted) and `(py/int-mod (- x start) step) = 0`.\n\n- **P3 | prelude.cljc:1010-1019 | Dict/set iteration observes insertions.** `py/iter-at` reads the live `:keys` vector, so `for k in d: d[k + 'x'] = 1` iterates unboundedly where CPython raises RuntimeError \"dictionary changed size during iteration\" (list iteration correctly stays live — that matches Python). **Fix:** snapshot `:keys` in `py/iterable` for dict/set, or track a size stamp and raise RuntimeError.\n\n- **P3 | prelude.cljc:618-631 | Float `//` and `%` deviate from CPython in the last ulp.** `floor(fl(x/y))` and `x - y·floor(x/y)` vs CPython's fmod-corrected exact-quotient algorithm: e.g. `5.9 % 1.1` → `0.40000000000000036` here vs `0.39999999999999947` in CPython. Uniform across the four hosts (determinism intact), fidelity off. **Fix:** document in the report/design notes as a subset deviation, or add the fmod correction.\n\n- **P3 | prelude.cljc:1229-1281, 398-405, 439-449 | Binding/lookup micro-deviations.** Builtins accept keyword arguments (`len(obj=[1])` succeeds; CPython: \"len() takes no keyword arguments\"); `C(1, 2)` with no `__init__` silently sets `.args` instead of TypeError; `py/getattr` finds dunders on instance attrs, while Python's implicit `with` invocation looks `__enter__`/`__exit__` up on the type (an instance-attr `__exit__` is honored here, ignored by CPython). All loud-or-benign edges; **fix:** add a `:no-kw` flag to builtin specs and a type-only dunder path in `py/with`, or record as accepted deviations.\n\nReport accuracy: the implementer's claims match the source on every point I could re-derive (rule table, prelude inventory, refusal/syntax lists, mutation M2b's added clamp cases `t[1:100]`, `'hello'[-100:2]`, `t[100:0:-1]` are present at e2e_c1_test.clj:186). Disclosed deviations (no counts in messages, insertion-ordered sets — within the mappability ruling, snapshot views, non-integral `**` as NotImplementedError, `(x) = 1` rejected) are accurate; dict-`==`-by-identity remains the earlier ruled scope item. CLJD sign-off is by reading only: the one new reader conditional (`render.cljc:46-50`) has `:cljd` first, no protocol methods were added; the orchestrator's CLJD lane remains the executing confirmation.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: WITHHELD\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
