{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"Focused probes on all four JVM VMs found three gaps: `any` evaluates a generator’s tail after the result is decided; exception constructors silently discard keywords; and range length can raise OverflowError when the result is only 2. I also found that `%` inherits the documented large-quotient limit for `//`; I’m checking that and range iteration across hosts.\n"}}
